        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(xai): add handshakeTimeout to TTS stream WebSocket",
        "body": "AI-assisted: yes. I reviewed and understand the change.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe xAI TTS stream creates `new WebSocket()` without `handshakeTimeout`. The existing `connectTimer` fires after `timeoutMs` and calls `failConnect()`, which **rejects the promise but does not close or terminate the WebSocket** — the underlying TCP connection and its memory remain occupied. The `handshakeTimeout` at the ws library level cleans up the TCP connection when the HTTP→WebSocket upgrade stalls.\n\nThe voice bridge was excluded: its `connectTimeout` already calls `ws.terminate()`, which the pinned ws library aborts the active request and destroys the socket even in CONNECTING state.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`handshakeTimeout: timeoutMs` (30 s default) — passes the existing timeout parameter to the ws constructor so the library itself enforces the upgrade deadline and releases TCP resources.\n\n## User Impact\n\nStalled xAI TTS connections now release TCP resources within their configured timeout instead of leaking them until GC. Healthy connections are unaffected.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Before vs After (controlled stalled WebSocket upgrade)\n\nA TCP server accepts but stalls the upgrade (partial HTTP 101, no terminating `\\r\\n`):\n\n```json\n{\"label\":\"BEFORE (default=0, unlimited)\",\"handshakeTimeoutMs\":0,\"outcome\":\"REJECTED\",\"error\":\"aborted after 5000ms\",\"elapsed_ms\":5016}\n{\"label\":\"AFTER (5 s)\",\"handshakeTimeoutMs\":5000,\"outcome\":\"REJECTED\",\"error\":\"Opening handshake has timed out\",\"elapsed_ms\":5015}\n```\n\n- **BEFORE**: `handshakeTimeout=0` → still hanging at 5 s (aborted externally).\n- **AFTER**: `\"Opening handshake has timed out\"` at 5015 ms — terminated within deadline.\n\n### Why only TTS (not voice bridge)\n\n| Function | Existing timeout mechanism | Cleans up TCP? | handshakeTimeout needed? |\n|------|------|------|------|\n| `xaiTTSStream` | `connectTimer → failConnect()` | **No** — only rejects promise | ✅ Yes |\n| `XaiRealtimeVoiceBridge` | `connectTimeout → ws.terminate()` | Yes — terminate() destroys socket | ❌ No (reverted) |\n\n### Focused tests\n\n```\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/xai/tts.test.ts --run\nTest Files  1 passed (1)  Tests  26 passed (26)\n\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/xai/realtime-voice-provider.test.ts --run\nTest Files  1 passed (1)  Tests  36 passed (36)\n```\n\n- `expect(ws?.handshakeTimeout).toBe(5_000)` — timeoutMs reaches ws constructor.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
        "branch": "codex/fix-xai-ws-handshake-timeout",
